---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import MoreTools from '../components/content/MoreTools.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, createWebPageSchema } from '../data/schemas';

const breadcrumb = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy-policy/' },
]);

const lastUpdated = 'October 18, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Yes No Button"
  description="Privacy policy for the Yes No Button, including how browser storage, analytics, advertising, and hosting services may process data."
  canonical="https://yesnobuttonapp.com/privacy-policy/"
  schema={[createWebPageSchema("Privacy policy for the Yes No Button, including how browser storage, analytics, advertising, and hosting services may process data.", 'https://yesnobuttonapp.com/privacy-policy/', 'Privacy Policy'), breadcrumb]}
>
  <Fragment slot="header"><Header /></Fragment>

  <section class="py-[80px] max-sm:py-[48px] bg-[#FAFAF8] dark:bg-canvas-dark">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-6">
        <a href="/about/" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-card-dark border border-border dark:border-border-dark text-muted dark:text-muted-dark hover:text-ink dark:hover:text-ink-dark transition-colors no-underline">About</a>
        <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-btn-bg dark:bg-btn-bg-dark text-btn-text dark:text-btn-text-dark border border-btn-bg dark:border-btn-bg-dark no-underline">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/terms/" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-card-dark border border-border dark:border-border-dark text-muted dark:text-muted-dark hover:text-ink dark:hover:text-ink-dark transition-colors no-underline">Terms</a>
        <a href="/disclaimer/" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-card-dark border border-border dark:border-border-dark text-muted dark:text-muted-dark hover:text-ink dark:hover:text-ink-dark transition-colors no-underline">Disclaimer</a>
        <a href="/contact/" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-card-dark border border-border dark:border-border-dark text-muted dark:text-muted-dark hover:text-ink dark:hover:text-ink-dark transition-colors no-underline">Contact</a>
      </div>
      <span class="block text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.1em] text-[#16A34A] uppercase mb-2.5">PRIVACY POLICY</span>
      <h1 class="font-display text-[36px] max-sm:text-[28px] font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark leading-[1.15] mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-muted-dark text-sm mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="text-muted dark:text-muted-dark space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Introduction</h2>
          <p>At YesNoButton ("we", "our", or "us"), we take your privacy seriously. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you visit our website at yesnobuttonapp.com (the "Service").</p>
          <p>We believe in minimal data collection. The Yes No Button itself is designed to run in your browser. We do not run an account system, and we do not store your questions or answers on our own servers.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>The Yes No Button tool runs client-side in your browser using JavaScript. When you press the button:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mt-2">
            <li>Your typed question is not sent to our servers</li>
            <li>The result is generated locally in your browser</li>
            <li>We do not create user accounts or ask for personal profile information</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">The only data that may be stored is your history of results in your browser's <code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-border/30 dark:bg-border-dark/30 text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">localStorage</code>. This data never leaves your device and can be cleared at any time using the "Clear history" option in the tool.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Cookies and Tracking</h2>
          <p>When you first visit, a cookie banner lets you accept or reject analytics and advertising cookies. In the EU, UK and Switzerland these stay off until you accept. We save your choice in your browser's localStorage so we do not ask again, and you can change it any time with the "Cookie Settings" link in the footer.</p>
          <p>Some articles include embedded YouTube videos. These load only after you press play, and they use YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com). Once a video loads, YouTube and Google may collect information under their own privacy policies.</p>
          <p>We use local browser storage to remember preferences such as your selected theme and result history. This information stays on your device.</p>
          <p>We use Google Analytics to understand aggregate website usage, such as page views, device types, and general traffic patterns. Google may use cookies or similar technologies to provide this service.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">What We Store in Your Browser</h2>
          <p>Everything in this table is kept in your own browser using localStorage. None of it is sent to our servers, and you can remove all of it by clearing site data in your browser settings.</p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto mt-3">
            <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
              <thead><tr><th class="text-left text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-semibold px-3 py-2 border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Key</th><th class="text-left text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-semibold px-3 py-2 border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">What it is for</th><th class="text-left text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-semibold px-3 py-2 border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">How long it stays</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark"><code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-border/30 dark:bg-border-dark/30 text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">theme</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Remembers your light, dark or system theme choice.</td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Until you clear it</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark"><code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-border/30 dark:bg-border-dark/30 text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">ynb_history</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Your recent Yes, No and Maybe results, shown in the history panel. Never sent to us.</td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Until you press Clear history or clear browser data</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark"><code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-border/30 dark:bg-border-dark/30 text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">ynb_mode</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Whether you last used Yes/No or Yes/No/Maybe mode.</td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Until you clear browser data</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark"><code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-border/30 dark:bg-border-dark/30 text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">ynb_consent</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Your cookie choice (accepted or rejected), so we do not ask again.</td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Until you clear it or change it in Cookie Settings</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark"><code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-border/30 dark:bg-border-dark/30 text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">ynb_toy_seen</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Records that you have already seen the first-visit tap hint on the homepage button.</td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Until you clear browser data</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark"><code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-border/30 dark:bg-border-dark/30 text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">ynb_uses</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">A simple counter of how many results you have generated, used only to decide when to offer the bookmark or home screen prompt.</td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Until you clear browser data</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark"><code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-border/30 dark:bg-border-dark/30 text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">ynb_install_dismissed</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">The time you closed the bookmark or home screen prompt, so we do not show it again for 30 days.</td><td class="px-3 py-2 align-top border-b border-border dark:border-border-dark">Until you clear browser data</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Bookmarking, Home Screen and Offline Use</h2>
          <p>You can bookmark the site or add it to your phone's home screen. When you visit, the site may register a small service worker. This is a script that stores copies of our own pages, images and sounds in your browser so the button opens faster and keeps working with a poor connection.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The service worker only handles files from yesnobuttonapp.com. It does not store or intercept requests to Google Analytics, Google AdSense or other third parties, and it does not record what you ask. You can remove it by clearing site data or uninstalling the home screen icon.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Embedded Widget</h2>
          <p>Website owners can embed the Yes No Button on their own pages using an iframe that loads yesnobuttonapp.com/embed/. That page contains only the button. It does not load our analytics or advertising scripts. Like the main site, it can keep your result history in your browser's localStorage. The website that embeds the widget has its own privacy practices, which we do not control.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>Our website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare may process standard web server logs, such as IP address, browser type, pages requested, and security events, for hosting, security, and performance purposes.</p>
          <p>We use Google AdSense to display advertising. Google and its partners may use cookies, device identifiers, or similar technologies to serve and measure ads, prevent fraud, and comply with advertising policies. Depending on your location and Google settings, ads may be personalized or non-personalized.</p>
          <p>We use Google Analytics to measure site performance and understand usage trends. Analytics data is used in aggregate to improve the website.</p>
          <p>The tool may use your browser's built-in speech synthesis feature to read results aloud. This is handled by your device or browser.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Data Retention</h2>
          <p>We do not retain your typed questions or generated answers on our own servers. Any result history stored in your browser's localStorage is under your control and can be deleted at any time.</p>
          <p>Third-party services such as Google and Cloudflare may retain data according to their own privacy policies and retention practices.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Your Choices and Rights</h2>
          <p>You can control your data in several ways:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mt-2">
            <li>Change or withdraw your cookie choice at any time with <strong>Cookie Settings</strong> in the footer</li>
            <li>Clear your result history with <strong>Clear history</strong> in the tool</li>
            <li>Clear cookies and site data in your browser settings</li>
            <li>Manage Google ad personalisation at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark underline hover:no-underline" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Ad Settings</a></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, you may also have the right to object to or restrict processing, to receive a copy of your data, and to complain to your local data protection authority. If you are in California, you may have the right to know what is collected and to opt out of certain sharing of personal information for advertising. Because we hold almost no personal data ourselves, most of these requests are best directed at Google or Cloudflare, but you are welcome to <a href="/contact/" class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark underline hover:no-underline">contact us</a> and we will help where we can.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>Our Service is safe for children and complies with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and similar regulations. We do not knowingly collect any personal information from children under the age of 13 (or the equivalent age in your jurisdiction).</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark mb-3">Contact</h2>
          <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please <a href="/contact/" class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark underline hover:no-underline">contact us</a>.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <MoreTools />

  <Fragment slot="footer"><Footer /></Fragment>
</BaseLayout>
